before:
Compile javac --release 25 -d classes Main.java tools/Scale.java; run java -cp classes Main. A real third-party build should record dependency versions and repositories, not rely on an accidental IDE class path. Here the exact helper is:
```java
package tools;
public class Scale {
  public static int doubleIt(int value) { return value * 2; }
}
```

Complete local Java example; the app itself does not execute it:
```java
import tools.Scale;
public class Main {

  public static void main(String[] args) {
    System.out.println(Scale.doubleIt(6));
  }
}
```

after:
Save each labeled part separately. Follow Main's call into the supplied helper method.

```java
// File: tools/Scale.java
package tools;
public class Scale {
  public static int doubleIt(int value) { return value * 2; }
}

// File: Main.java
import tools.Scale;
public class Main {

  public static void main(String[] args) {
    System.out.println(Scale.doubleIt(6));
  }
}
```
